@jayyuen66/dsh-dir-prep-organize README · <img src="https://api.iconify.design/lucide/network.svg?color=%23658EFF&height=22" height="22" width="22" align="absmiddle" alt="" /> Public interface：- Business failures stay `ok:false` with `error`. The import path-policy branches are the exception: an out-of-bounds path or a malformed `path` field also carries `status` 403 or 400.
- `model` is the preflight read of the default selection; `organize` prefers the live agent's selection as described under "The polish call".
- Result parsing on the client keeps defensive defaults: a non-object payload or a missing `ok:true` becomes a **visible error**, never an empty list.

